# A frame a C jump's unwind collects from holds no byte AddressSanitizer
# poisons (panel 258's R2; design.md §1.12; `emit/unwind_scope.hero` decides
# which frames, `runtime/parts/unwind.c` is the mechanism).
#
# **WHY.** Before R2 no Heroes frame held a local whose address is taken: a
# value of 4 KiB or more lives in the room off the frame and every other one
# in a slot clang may keep in a register, so ASan gave a Heroes frame no
# redzone, and a C library that copies a coroutine's stack out to the heap
# and back read every byte of one under `--sanitize` (panel 259's
# `run/fixedbugs-coroutines-copied-out-and-in-of-one-carved-region-each-keep-their-large-values`).
# R2's slots and marks are declared with a cleanup, which takes their address,
# so ASan put redzones around them, and that program's header, copying the
# region with `memcpy`, was stopped by ASan at `--sanitize -O0`
# (stack-buffer-underflow, 3 runs of 3, this lane, 2026-11-27), a correct
# program refused by the instrument. A cleanup that only reads its slot's
# value does not help: at `-O0` clang inlines nothing, even an
# `always_inline` cleanup's pointer is stored in a slot of its own, and the
# slot stays instrumented (read in clang's IR that day).
#
# **WHICH FUNCTIONS.** A function whose prologue writes the unwind's mark,
# which every frame with a collected slot or a residue carries
# (`unwind_scope.frame_mark`), and every thunk of a program that unwinds,
# which carries its own mark (`unwind_scope.thunk_mark`). Their definitions
# open with `__no_sanitize__("address")`, so no redzone exists in such a
# frame, as none did before R2.
#
# **WHAT IT COSTS.** The checks ASan adds to such a function's own loads and
# stores, in a program that hands a function to a C library's group and only
# under `--sanitize`. The runtime's functions, the headers' and every other
# function of the program keep theirs, and a use after free of a value C reads
# at its catch is still told in the C that reads it. The word is spelled as C
# reserves it, so no group's header can define it as a macro
# (`emit/guarded_names.hero`'s list holds `__no_sanitize__`).

use emit/ctype
use emit/unwind_scope

# Spelled as C reserves it.
constant UNSANITIZED: str
    "__attribute__((__no_sanitize__(\"address\"))) "

# The words a definition opens with: the attribute where the frame carries a
# mark, nothing elsewhere.
function words(marked: bool) -> str
    if marked
        return UNSANITIZED
    return ""

# The words a thunk's definition opens with: the attribute in a program that
# unwinds, where every thunk carries the mark below.
function thunk_words(names: ctype.Names) -> str
    return words(marked: unwind_scope.unwinds(names))

# What a thunk's first line carries after its entry in a program that
# unwinds, "" in any other: a mark whose cleanup ends the callback's count as
# one unwound where an unwind leaves the thunk, and does nothing on its return,
# initialised by the call that opens the program to the runtime's hook, which
# walks no other program's stack (`hero_unwind_handed`). The mark holds the
# number the runtime gives this activation of the thunk, and the runtime
# learns, from the mark's address, its frame's and the thunk's own (`thunk`,
# its C name), where the mark lies in every activation of that code: a group
# tells the frames below a thunk by that number, so a C library that copies
# two coroutines' stacks in turn through one region, the frames of both at
# the same addresses, no longer has the one's return release what the
# other's catch still reads (`runtime/parts/unwind.c`, `hero_unwind_same`;
# this lane's probe, 2026-11-27: ASan's heap use after free, 3 runs of 3).
function thunk_mark(names: ctype.Names, thunk: str) -> str
    if !unwind_scope.unwinds(names)
        return ""
    handed = "hero_unwind_handed(&hero_unwound, __builtin_frame_address(0), (void (*)(void))" + thunk + ");"
    return " HERO_NODEBUG uint64_t hero_unwound " + unwind_scope.CLEANUP + "hero_unwind_thunk))) = " + handed

test "a frame with a mark is left uninstrumented, any other is written as it was"
    assert words(marked: true) == "__attribute__((__no_sanitize__(\"address\"))) "
    assert words(marked: false) == ""
